Person re-identification, a critical task in computer vision, aims to identify individuals across cameras with a wide field of view. Current methods primarily focus on local and global feature alignment, but often overlook critical information such as person attributes. Our research introduces a new technique that aligns features based on person clusters and attributes, leveraging both global and local features. We propose a joint learning method that simultaneously trains a person attribute classifier and a person re-ID model. Our approach improves upon existing state-of-the-art methods by incorporating attribute information, achieving superior results on standard benchmarks. Furthermore, we demonstrate the effectiveness of our method in real-world scenarios through experiments on large, unlabelled datasets. Our results show that our method excels in challenging, unlabelled re-ID scenarios, outperforming top-performing methods. Our code and a pre-trained model are available for public use on the GitHub platform. The project's website can be found at https://github.com/ChenyuYan2019/ClusterNet. \end{document} 

